<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paris Lodron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1586–<a href="/years/1653">1653</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Lodron was prince-archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> from 1619 to 1653. Through careful neutrality and new fortifications he kept the archbishopric out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>. He consecrated the rebuilt Salzburg Cathedral in 1628 and founded the University of Salzburg in 1622.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris-lodron.jpg" alt="Paris Lodron" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joannes Jenet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_Lodron_G_1062_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
